#ident	"@(#)uucp:Permissions	2.2"
# This entry for public login.
# It provides the default permissions.
# See the Basic Networking Utilities Guide for more information.
# 
# Each line can contain the following options:
# 
# LOGNAME=  
#	For incoming calls only.  This is the login name a remote system can 
#	use to log into your system.  A line that starts with LOGNAME specifies
#	the permissions a remote "user" has on your system.
#
# MACHINE=
#	For outgoing calls only.  This entry is the name of a machine
#	you can call.  A line that starts with MACHINE specifies the
#	permissions you have on the remote system.  
#
# REQUEST= 
#	Determines whether a remote system can transfer files from your system.
#	No is the default answer.
#
# CALLBACK=
#	Used with LOGNAME entries.  If it =yes, your system must call back
#	the remote system before transferring files.  The remote system makes
#	the request, but your system must call it back. 
#
# SENDFILES=
#	Used with LOGNAME entries.  Specifies whether the remote system can 
# 	take work that you have queued for it.  If it =yes, you can send the
#	queued work to the remote system.  If it =call, you can only send the 
#	files when you initiate the call.  call is the default.
#
# READ= WRITE=
#	These are the places where uucico can read and write files.  The
#	default for both is /var/spool/uucppublic.  Separate multiple paths
#	with commas. 
#
# COMMANDS= 
#	Used with MACHINE entries.  Specifies commands a remote system can run
#	on your system.  You can specify paths to commands.  Separate commands
#	with a comma.  	
#
# See The "System Administrator's Guide, Basic Networking Utilites" for more
# information.  	
	
LOGNAME=nuucp REQUEST=yes CALLBACK=no SENDFILES=yes READ=/ WRITE=/usr/spool/uucppublic
LOGNAME=uucp REQUEST=yes CALLBACK=no SENDFILES=yes READ=/ WRITE=/usr/spool/uucppublic
LOGNAME=OTHER REQUEST=yes CALLBACK=no SENDFILES=yes READ=/ WRITE=/usr/spool/uucppublic
MACHINE=OTHER REQUEST=yes CALLBACK=no SENDFILES=yes READ=/ WRITE=/usr/spool/uucppublic COMMANDS=rnews:rmail:uucp
